      "name": "How do I prepare my trees for storm season?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Walk your property in spring before severe-storm season starts. Inspect every mature tree within striking distance (roughly tree height) of your house, garage, fence, pool, or driveway. Look for sudden lean, vertical trunk cracks, fungal conks at the base, large dead branches over targets, co-dominant leaders, and disease symptoms such as EAB on ash and oak wilt on oak. Schedule pruning or removal for anything structurally compromised. That 30-60 minute walk-around in April prevents most preventable storm damage." }
    },
