      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I do if a tree falls on my house?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Make sure everyone is safe and stay away from the tree until you have checked for power lines. Photograph everything before cleanup starts, then tarp any roof breach to prevent water intrusion. Call your homeowners insurance claims line within 24 hours, and call Roubic's emergency line at {{global.phone}} for extraction. Do not attempt DIY removal — storm-damaged trees have unpredictable spring tension and are the leading cause of tree-related fatalities nationally." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does homeowners insurance cover storm-damage tree removal?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Generally yes, when a tree damages a covered structure such as a house, garage, certain fences, or a vehicle in some scenarios. Insurance typically does not cover removal of a tree that fell without damaging anything, or routine removal of a healthy tree. Roubic provides the documentation carriers want — photos, itemized work, species and diameter estimates — built into the storm-response workflow so your claim moves through cleanly." }
    },
