      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the most common tree-storm-failure mode in NE Ohio?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "EAB-killed ash failing without visible warning is the most common single failure mode in NE Ohio right now — brittle dead wood snaps in even moderate winds. After that, co-dominant leaders splitting at the V, followed by root-plate failure on shallow-rooted species like silver maple, willow, and Norway maple on saturated ground. Pre-season inspection catches all three categories." }
